From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poyu Chen <me@poyu.xyz>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:50:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: add a battery and charger driver for the Zebra
 WT41N0

The WT41N0 charges its battery with the TWL6030's own charger; nothing in the
kernel enables it, so the battery never charges. Do what the stock OS does:
switch the charger's input with the External Agent's charge path "fuses" (the
cradle supply or USB VBUS), program and enable the charger (4.2 V; 700 mA from
the cradle, 500 mA from USB), keep its watchdog fed and its settings in place,
and stop when no power source is present, the battery is missing, or its
temperature is outside 0-45 C.

Battery presence, temperature, charge current and the cradle power state come
from the External Agent microcontroller, the battery voltage from the PMIC ADC.
Charging, full and fault states are reported as a power supply; while
charging, the EA's charge LED (the middle LED) blinks orange, as in the stock
OS.

Upstream: not submitted
